            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "The VIIRS active fire dataset provides fire detections at a 375 m spatial resolution, offering enhanced sensitivity to smaller and low-intensity fires compared to legacy sensors. This higher spatial resolution improves the detection of early-stage ignitions and fragmented fire events, which are common in savanna ecosystems such as Kainji Lake National Park. Consequently, VIIRS data were used as the primary source for assigning daily fire occurrence labels in the machine learning framework, with emphasis placed on medium- and high-confidence detections to minimize false positives.",
